language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member selected the Spec tab of the right panel of a View in the Workbench; the panel is 340px wide at the right edge and scrolls (the Decisions and References, and the Requirements, are Views of their own).","The base state is the View Checkout for a member who may write Views on a desktop layout: every section authored, a pencil on each.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; a tablet reads the document and says \"Edit on desktop\", and below 640px a phone reads it with §1 open and the other sections folded behind their titles."],"intent":"Show the Spec tab of a View's right panel as built from Adapter Widgets only, the first half of the document: the View's intent, entry conditions, interaction rules, constraints and accessibility notes as numbered sections with their counts, the pencil that edits one section on a desktop layout, and the dashed placeholders of a section that is empty.","interactionRules":["The document is the View's Spec: mono section markers (§1 to §8), the section title with the number of items, and the authored prose at a 68ch measure with a hairline between sections.","A `#widget-id` in the prose that names a Widget of this View is a link that selects the Widget on the canvas.","A pencil edits one section at a time, on a desktop layout and only for a member who may write Views; while a section is being edited the other pencils are disabled.","An empty section is said so in a dashed placeholder, with Add for a member who may edit it; a tablet and a phone offer no editing, and a member without the key is offered neither pencil nor Add.","The Spec is stated explicitly, including when a section is empty; whether it is complete is judged by Checks and Review, not by which sections have content."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"deci